						Co-presented with Rizel Scarlett (GitHub).
					</p>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<!-- 2021 -->
		<section
			class="mb-14 grid scroll-mt-24 gap-x-10 gap-y-2 border-t border-surface-4 pt-5 md:grid-cols-[clamp(140px,16vw,240px)_1fr]"
			id="2021"
		>
			<h2 class="font-display text-[clamp(64px,9vw,140px)] leading-[0.85] font-normal text-pink md:sticky md:top-24 md:self-start">
				2021
			</h2>
			<ul class="space-y-7">
				<li>
					<h3 class="text-[clamp(19px,1.6vw,23px)] leading-snug font-semibold text-paper">
						<a
							href="https://www.conf42.com/Cloud_Native_2021_Joe_Karlsson_save_the_world_data_lakes"
							target="_blank"
							rel="noopener noreferrer"
							class={LINK}
						>
							Save The World And Money with MongoDB Data Lakes
						</a>
					</h3>
					<p class="mt-1 text-sm text-muted">
						Conf42 Cloud Native 2021 · April 29th, 2021 (virtual)
					</p>
					<p class="mt-1 text-muted">
						Using MongoDB's Data Lake service to auto-archive cold data to AWS S3 while maintaining
						query capabilities - reducing data center power consumption and costs.
					</p>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<!-- 2020 -->
		<section
			class="mb-14 grid scroll-mt-24 gap-x-10 gap-y-2 border-t border-surface-4 pt-5 md:grid-cols-[clamp(140px,16vw,240px)_1fr]"
			id="2020"
		>
			<h2 class="font-display text-[clamp(64px,9vw,140px)] leading-[0.85] font-normal text-pink md:sticky md:top-24 md:self-start">
